      "worked_solution": "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $10\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+10\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-10\\text{i},$ or simply $-10\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-10\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-7+6\\text{i}}{10\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-7+6\\text{i}}{10\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-10\\text{i}}{-10\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{70\\text{i}-60{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-100{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{70\\text{i}-60(-1)}{-100(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{60+70\\text{i}}{100}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{60+70\\text{i}}{100} & =\\frac{60}{100}+\\frac{70}{100}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{7}{10}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
